GREEN for reviewFilter (30 tests). Now RED phase 3: the runner wiring in `postPReviewComments.js`. Tests for:
1. The filter gate: verification=filter + candidates → CLI invoked, prompt written, verdicts applied, census recomputed, general comment injection written, stats logged.
2. verification=none → byte-identical legacy behavior (no CLI, no census recompute).
3. Zero candidates → no CLI run.
4. CLI failure / missing filter output → non-fatal, unfiltered flow continues.
5. Demote on a file-referenced comment rewrites the comment file with the demotion note.
6. Dropped section appended to the general comment file.

For unit tests I'll test the exported helpers:
- `reviewFilterEnabled(policy)` 
- `runReviewFilter(reviewData, ctx)` — the orchestration, with injectable cli executor for tests. Look at how existing code handles cli_execute_command injection: `attemptResumeIfReviewOutputsMissing` calls the global directly — tests must mock the global via the globalMock bag (loadModule's third arg). In test_postPReviewComments.js the loader passes globals {file_read: ...} — I can add cli_execute_command to that bag.

Design of the runner functions (in postPReviewComments.js):

```js
function verificationEnabled(policy) { return !!policy && policy.verification === 'filter'; }

function filterInputPath() { return 'outputs/' + reviewFilterModule.INPUT_FILE; }
function filterOutputPath() { return 'outputs/' + reviewFilterModule.OUTPUT_FILE; }
function filterPromptPath() { return 'outputs/.pr-review-filter-prompt.md'; }

function resolveFilterClaim(inlineComment, ticketKey, workingDir) → resolveInlineComment(inlineComment, ticketKey, workingDir)

function writeFilterInputFile(candidates) — writeFile(filterInputPath(), buildFilterInputJson(candidates))
function writeFilterPromptFile(diffPath) — writeFile(promptPath, buildFilterPrompt(diffPath))

function runFilterCli(workingDir) — cli_execute_command({command: 'bash agents/scripts/run-agent.sh ' + promptPath, workingDirectory?}) → boolean (false on throw)
function readFilterVerdicts(ticketKey, workingDir) — outputFiles.readOutputFileDetailed(OUTPUT_FILE, {...}) → raw string | null
function applyVerdictNotesToFiles(aplied, ticketKey, workingDir) — for demotes: if inlineComment.comment (file) → read current content, append note, writeFile. Body-inline: applyFilterVerdicts didn't append to body — WAIT, design decision earlier: pure apply sets severity; note returned in applied[i].note. The RUNER must append the note to body (inline) or file (comment path). But applyFilterVerdicts already ran and I need the inlineComment reference for the note... The applied entries carry id — map id → original inline comment object? After drops, indices shift; the inline entries carry __filterId temporarily... but apply removes the tags at the end. Hmm — cleaner: the pure apply should attach the note onto the inline comment ITSELF: for inline bodies append there; for file-referenced... the pure module can't write files but CAN set a marker the runner reads: inlineComment.__filterNote = note? JSON-safety: it's in-memory only, and the runner strips it after handling. 

Actually — simplest correct approach: pure apply appends the note to `inlineComment.body` when body is a string (inline case — done in pure module), and for the file case the RUNER handles: after apply, for each applied demote entry with path+line, find the matching inline comment (by path+line+severity===to) and rewrite its comment FILE with the appended note. Let me restructure: pure applyFilterVerdicts:
- demote: inline[idx].severity = tier; if (typeof inline[idx].body === 'string' && inline[idx].body) inline[idx].body += '\n' + note; inline[idx].__filterNote = note (marker for the file-rewrite pass). Return applied entry WITHOUT note (the note lives on the comment).
- runner: after apply, walk applied demote entries → locate inline comment by __filterNote → if inlineComment.comment (file path): read file content (readMarkdownFile), append note, writeFile; then delete inlineComment.__filterNote.

Hmm — resolveInlineComment gives "body wins else file". After appending to the FILE, posting reads body?? body is empty for file-referenced comments (comment field). Posting: rawInlineTextOf = body || readMarkdownFile(comment) → file content (with note). Good.

Simpler alternative: runner-side append via applied entries carrying path+line+to+note; find in reviewData.inlineComments the entry with that path/line whose severity === applied.to. Path/line collisions possible but rare; __filterId marker is deterministic. Let me keep __filterId approach: pure apply tags the inline comment objects with `__filterId` and leaves the tags ON (removing them at the end was my current code — I'll keep the tags removal but ALSO set __filterNote). The runner pass:
``
function stampDemotionNotes(reviewData, applied, ticketKey, workingDir) {
 applied.filter(a => a.decision === 'demote').forEach(a => {
    var inline = findInlineByFilterId(reviewData, a.id);
    if (!inline) return;
    if (inline.comment) { // file-referenced
       var content = readMarkdownFile(inline.comment, ticketKey, workingDir);
       if (content) writeFile(inline.comment, content.replace(/\s*$/, '') + '\n' + a.note + '\n');
    }
    delete inline.__filterId; delete inline.__filterNote... 
 });
}
``
Wait — but the pure module currently strips __filterId at the end. Change: pure apply KEEPS __filterId on the inline objects (runner deletes them after handling). Hmm — but then if the filter didn't run... the tags only exist when apply ran. The posting path would carry __filterId fields into... nothing — inline comments are read field-wise by the poster (path/line/body/comment/severity). Extra fields harmless. But findingsFromReviewData copies specific fields — harmless too. Still, cleaner to delete. I'll keep tags on and delete in the runner's stampDemotionNotes (which iterates ALL inline entries deleting __filterId). 

Edge: pure apply appends note to body for INLINE bodies — so runner only handles the FILE case + tag cleanup.

Actually wait — should the demote note go into the inline body even when a comment file exists? Posting prefers body. For file-referenced comments body is absent → note must go to the file. OK.

7. `applyReviewFilter(reviewData, ctx)` orchestration:
``
function applyReviewFilter(reviewData, ctx) {
 try {
   if (!verificationEnabled(ctx.reviewPolicy)) return null;
   var resolveClaim = function(c) { return resolveInlineComment(c, ctx.ticketKey, ctx.workingDir); };
   var candidates = reviewFilterModule.selectFilterCandidates(reviewData, ctx.reviewPolicy, resolveClaim);
   if (candidates.length === 0) { console.log('🧯 review filter (gh-1403): 0 candidates (no rework/polish-tier threads) — filter skipped'); return null; }
   writeFilterInputFile(candidates);
   writeFilterPromptFile(diffPathOf(ctx));
   var ran = runFilterCli(ctx.workingDir);
   if (!ran) { console.warn('🧯 review filter CLI failed — running unfiltered (gh-1403 fail-open)'); return null; }
   var raw = readFilterVerdicts(ctx.ticketKey, ctx.workingDir);
   if (!raw) { console.warn('🧯 no filter verdicts file — running unfiltered'); return null; }
   var parsed = reviewFilterModule.parseFilterVerdicts(raw);
   parsed.notes.forEach(n => console.warn('🧯 ' + n));
   var result = reviewFilterModule.applyFilterVerdicts(reviewData, candidates, parsed.verdicts);
   result.notes.forEach(n => console.warn('🧯 ' + n));
   stampDemotionNotes(reviewData, result.aplied, ctx.ticketKey, ctx.workingDir);
   cleanupFilterTags(reviewData);
   var census = reviewFilterModule.recomputeCensus(reviewData, result.dropped.length);
   reviewData.issueCounts = census; // census recomputed AFTER filtering
   var stats = reviewFilterModule.filterStats(candidates.length, result.aplied);
   logFilterOutcome(stats, reviewFilterModule.buildOverSupressionWarning(stats));
   injectDroppedIntoGeneralComment(reviewData, stats, result.dropped, ctx.ticketKey, ctx.workingDir);
   return { stats: stats, dropped: result.dropped, applied: result.aplied };
 } catch (e) {
   console.warn('🧯 review filter failed (non-fatal, running unfiltered): ' + (e.message || e));
   return null;
 }
``

- diffPathOf(ctx): the filter prompt references the diff — the review run's input folder: inputFolderPath param + '/pr_diff.txt'. ctx has inputFolderPath? action(params) — ctx built from params: buildReviewContext keeps jp/ticketKey/etc. — inputFolderPath is params.inputFolderPath. I'll pass diffPath = (params.inputFolderPath ? params.inputFolderPath + '/pr_diff.txt' : 'pr_diff.txt'). Pass into ctx.filterDiffPath at action level.

- injectDroppedIntoGeneralComment: generalComment is a path (contract). Resolve: if it matches the outputs-path regex (reuse resolveCommentFileReference's regex shape — but that READS content; I need the path check): 
``
function appendDroppedSection(reviewData, section, ticketKey, workingDir) {
 var path = typeof reviewData.generalComment === 'string' ? reviewData.generalComment.trim() : null;
 if (!path || !/^(outputs\/)?[\w.\-\/]+\.md$/.test(path)) return false; // inline or unknown → skip
 var content = readMarkdownFile(path, ticketKey, workingDir);
 if (!content) return false;
 writeFile(path, content.replace(/\s*$/, '') + '\n' + section + '\n');
 return true;
}
``
Reuse the existing regex from resolveCommentFileReference: `/^(outputs\/)?(pr_review_comments\/)?[\w.\-]+\.md$/` — that doesn't allow nested dirs beyond pr_review_comments. The generalComment is typically 'outputs/pr_review_general.md'. I'll use that same regex (consistency).

- stats also into the tracker stamp: postReviewToJira — add filterStampSection(m, filterOutcome): when outcome exists → one line + dropped count. Wire: action() stores outcome into a variable and passes to postReviewToJira. postReviewToJira signature currently (tracker, ticketKey, reviewContent, reviewData, prUrl, policy). Add a 7th param filterOutcome — update the call. Census lines in the tracker comment come from normalizeIssueCounts(reviewData) — recomputed values flow automatically since reviewData.issueCounts was replaced. 

Also result: buildSuccessResult includes filterOutcome? Add `filter: outcome.stats` when present — nice for CI logs. Optional; keep minimal: add to the returned result object (harmless).

- Wire in action(): after applySpecClaimDowngrades:
```js
// gh-1403: the finding-filter leg (reviewPolicy.verification = filter) — a
// fresh-context pass verifies each rework/polish-tier candidate before
// posting; drops become digest lines, demotes tier downgrades, the census
// is recomputed after filtering. Non-fatal: any filter failure degrades to
// the unfiltered review.
var filterOutcome = applyReviewFilter(reviewData, ctx, diffPathForFilter(params));
``
Then continue (normalizeRecommendation reads reviewData.issueCounts — recomputed). 

